   "RaceName": "State Representative Pos. 2",
   "Statement": "<b>Elected Experience</b><br><br>Pierce County Charter Review Commissioner elected in 2025, proudly representing County Council District 5.<br><br><b>Other Professional Experience</b><br></p><p></p><div><p><span>Jenn Marie is a small-business owner, home renovator, artist, and community leader. Jenn Marie is endorsed by the WA State Labor Council.<br></span></p></div><p><br><b>Education</b><br><br><span>An Orting High School grad, Jenn Marie is a proud alumna of Washington State University, where she attended on a rowing scholarship. She also attended Evergreen State College in Olympia.</span><br><br><b>Community Service</b><br><br><span>Jenn Marie is a rescue-dog mom who has served as a Family Promise board member and church deaconess, and she is an active member of the local Chamber of Commerce.</span></p><p><br><br><b>Statement</b><br><br><em><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">People. Power. Paychecks.&nbsp;</span></em><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Orting raised with small-town values: look out for neighbors, work hard, and never quit. Working </span><em><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">people</span></em><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">&nbsp;should be at the center of every decision made in Olympia.&nbsp;As your Charter Commissioner, I’m delivering </span><em><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">power</span></em><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">&nbsp;right now, including housing protections that keep seniors &amp; veterans in their homes.&nbsp;I’ll take the fight to Olympia to protect your </span><em><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">paycheck</span></em><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">&nbsp;from excessive costs for necessities: gas, groceries, and housing. I’ll champion local jobs that keep you close to home and out of gridlock, and I will work across the aisle to ensure the people’s interests are prioritized.</span></p><p><em><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">-Jenn Marie Strickling</span></em></p><p>&nbsp;</p><div><p>&nbsp;</p></div><p><br><br>",
